cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Agent Skills Compendium"
message: "If you use or reference this project, please cite the original project and author."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Milan"
    given-names: "Jerson Boyd"
    website: "https://jersonboydmilan.com/"

abstract: >-
  A structured framework for defining, organizing, discovering, and composing
  reusable capabilities for AI agents, built on the distinction between a tool
  (something an agent can use) and a skill (something an agent knows how to
  accomplish). Comprises a twenty-category taxonomy, a five-layer architectural
  model, and a canonical machine-readable skill specification.

keywords:
  - "AI agents"
  - "agent skills"
  - "capability registry"
  - "agent architecture"
  - "skill taxonomy"
  - "multi-agent systems"

repository-code: "https://github.com/jersonboydmilan/Agent-Skills-Compendium"
